<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <%- include('partials/head') %>
    <title>Documentation — OutRay</title>
    <style>
        .docs-wrapper {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: 280px 1fr;
            gap: 48px;
            padding-top: 140px;
            min-height: 100vh;
        }
        
        /* ── Sidebar ── */
        .docs-sidebar {
            position: sticky;
            top: 140px;
            height: calc(100vh - 140px);
            overflow-y: auto;
            border-right: 1px solid var(--border);
            padding-right: 24px;
        }
        .docs-sidebar::-webkit-scrollbar { width: 2px; }
        .docs-nav-group { margin-bottom: 32px; }
        .docs-nav-group h4 {
            font-size: 11px;
            font-weight: 700;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 1.5px;
            color: var(--muted);
            margin-bottom: 16px;
        }
        .docs-nav-link {
            display: block;
            padding: 8px 0;
            font-size: 14px;
            color: var(--text);
            text-decoration: none;
            transition: all 0.2s;
            opacity: 0.7;
        }
        .docs-nav-link:hover { opacity: 1; color: var(--accent); transform: translateX(4px); }
        .docs-nav-link.active { opacity: 1; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }

        /* ── Content ── */
        .docs-content {
            max-width: 800px;
            padding-bottom: 100px;
        }
        .docs-content section {
            padding: 40px 0 80px;
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
        }
        .docs-content section:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
        
        .docs-content h2 {
            font-size: 32px;
            font-weight: 800;
            letter-spacing: -1px;
            margin-bottom: 24px;
            color: #fff;
        }
        .docs-content h3 {
            font-size: 20px;
            font-weight: 700;
            margin-top: 40px;
            margin-bottom: 16px;
            color: var(--accent);
        }
        .docs-content p {
            font-size: 16px;
            color: var(--muted);
            margin-bottom: 24px;
            line-height: 1.8;
        }
        
        /* ── Code Blocks ── */
        .code-block {
            background: #08111f;
            border: 1px solid var(--border2);
            border-radius: 12px;
            padding: 24px;
            font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
            font-size: 14px;
            position: relative;
            margin: 32px 0;
            box-shadow: 0 20px 50px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);
        }
        .code-block::before {
            content: attr(data-lang);
            position: absolute;
            top: 12px;
            right: 16px;
            font-size: 10px;
            font-weight: 700;
            color: var(--muted);
            text-transform: uppercase;
        }
        .code-block pre { overflow-x: auto; color: #e2e8f0; }
        .code-block .comment { color: #4a5568; }
        .code-block .keyword { color: var(--accent3); }
        .code-block .string { color: var(--pink); }

        .note {
            background: rgba(79, 142, 247, 0.05);
            border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
            padding: 20px 24px;
            border-radius: 0 12px 12px 0;
            margin: 32px 0;
        }
        .note p { margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 15px; color: var(--text); }

        @media (max-width: 900px) {
            .docs-wrapper { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
            .docs-sidebar { display: none; }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <canvas id="net-canvas"></canvas>
    <%- include('partials/nav') %>

    <div class="container docs-wrapper">
        <!-- Sidebar -->
        <aside class="docs-sidebar">
            <div class="docs-nav-group">
                <h4>Getting Started</h4>
                <a href="#introduction" class="docs-nav-link active">Introduction</a>
                <a href="#installation" class="docs-nav-link">Installation</a>
                <a href="#authentication" class="docs-nav-link">Authentication</a>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-nav-group">
                <h4>Tunneling</h4>
                <a href="#http-tunnels" class="docs-nav-link">HTTP Tunnels</a>
                <a href="#custom-subdomains" class="docs-nav-link">Custom Subdomains</a>
                <a href="#request-inspect" class="docs-nav-link">Inspecting Requests</a>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-nav-group">
                <h4>Platform</h4>
                <a href="#organizations" class="docs-nav-link">Organizations</a>
                <a href="#api-tokens" class="docs-nav-link">API Tokens</a>
                <a href="#domains" class="docs-nav-link">Custom Domains</a>
            </div>
        </aside>

        <!-- Main Content -->
        <main class="docs-content">
            <section id="introduction">
                <div class="section-eyebrow">Docs</div>
                <h2>Introduction</h2>
                <p>Welcome to OutRay—the fastest way to bring your local server to the internet. Whether you're testing webhooks, sharing a demo with a client, or connecting mobile apps to your dev machine, OutRay provides a secure, HTTPS-ready tunnel in under a second.</p>
                <div class="note">
                    <p>💡 <strong>Free by Apcodesphere:</strong> All features of OutRay are completely free to use, including custom subdomains and organizational management.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="installation">
                <h2>Installation</h2>
                <p>OutRay is delivered as a lightweight CLI tool. You can install it using any major JavaScript package manager.</p>
                
                <h3>NPM</h3>
                <div class="code-block" data-lang="terminal">
                    <pre><span class="keyword">npm</span> install -g OutRay-cli</pre>
                </div>

                <h3>Yarn</h3>
                <div class="code-block" data-lang="terminal">
                    <pre><span class="keyword">yarn</span> global add OutRay-cli</pre>
                </div>

                <p>Once installed, verify the installation by running <code>OutRay --version</code> in your terminal.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="authentication">
                <h2>Authentication</h2>
                <p>To link your machine to your account and track your tunnels, you need to authenticate using your unique API token.</p>
                <ol style="margin-bottom: 24px; padding-left: 20px; color: var(--muted); line-height: 2;">
                    <li>Go to your <a href="/login" style="color: var(--accent);">OutRay Dashboard</a>.</li>
                    <li>Navigate to the <strong>API Tokens</strong> tab.</li>
                    <li>Copy your Default Token.</li>
                    <li>Run the login command in your terminal.</li>
                </ol>
                <div class="code-block" data-lang="terminal">
                    <pre><span class="keyword">OutRay</span> login YOUR_SECRET_TOKEN</pre>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="http-tunnels">
                <h2>HTTP Tunnels</h2>
                <p>Starting a tunnel is as simple as pointing the CLI to your local port. OutRay will automatically detect if you’re running a web server and generate a secure public URL.</p>
                
                <div class="code-block" data-lang="terminal">
                    <pre><span class="keyword">OutRay</span> start --port <span class="string">3000</span></pre>
                </div>

                <h3>Common Options</h3>
                <ul style="margin-bottom: 24px; padding-left: 20px; color: var(--muted); line-height: 2;">
                    <li><code>--port, -p</code> Specify the local port (Required)</li>
                    <li><code>--subdomain, -s</code> Request a custom subdomain</li>
                    <li><code>--protocol, -P</code> Use http or https (Default: https)</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section id="request-inspect">
                <h2>Request Inspector</h2>
                <p>OutRay includes a built-in inspector to help you debug incoming traffic. You can view all requests in real-time directly on the web dashboard under the <strong>Requests</strong> tab.</p>
                <p>You can see:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>HTTP Method and Path</li>
                    <li>Full Request Headers</li>
                    <li>JSON/Form Body Payloads</li>
                    <li>Response Status codes and Latency</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section id="organizations">
                <h2>Organizations</h2>
                <p>Working in a team? OutRay Organizations allow you to group tunnels, subdomains, and members under one entity.</p>
                <p>Created organizations have their own unique slugs (e.g., <code>OutRay.dev/dashboard/my-team</code>) making it easy to collaborate on project silos.</p>
            </section>
        </main>
    </div>

    <%- include('partials/footer') %>

    <script>
        // Smooth scroll for nav links
        document.querySelectorAll('.docs-nav-link').forEach(link => {
            link.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
                e.preventDefault();
                const target = document.querySelector(link.getAttribute('href'));
                window.scrollTo({
                    top: target.offsetTop - 120,
                    behavior: 'smooth'
                });
                
                // Update active state
                document.querySelectorAll('.docs-nav-link').forEach(l => l.classList.remove('active'));
                link.classList.add('active');
            });
        });

        // Intersection Observer to update sidebar on scroll
        const sections = document.querySelectorAll('.docs-content section');
        const navLinks = document.querySelectorAll('.docs-nav-link');

        window.addEventListener('scroll', () => {
            let current = "";
            sections.forEach(section => {
                const sectionTop = section.offsetTop;
                if (pageYOffset >= sectionTop - 150) {
                    current = section.getAttribute('id');
                }
            });

            navLinks.forEach(link => {
                link.classList.remove('active');
                if (link.getAttribute('href').includes(current)) {
                    link.classList.add('active');
                }
            });
        });

        gsap.from('.docs-sidebar', {opacity:0, x:-40, duration:1, ease:'power3.out'});
        gsap.from('.docs-content', {opacity:0, y:40, duration:1, ease:'power3.out', delay:0.2});
        
        <%- include('partials/network_js') %>
    </script>
</body>
</html>
